<p>Then there is the age limit. Honestly, the age limit is the biggest stress factor for older aspirants. Generally, the age bracket is 18 to 30 years old. A few specific posts might stretch it to 32 years, and some lower level posts might cap it at 27. It really depends. But if you fall under a reserved category, you get some breathing room. OBC candidates get an extra 3 years. SC and ST candidates get an extra 5 years. If you are a Person with Benchmark Disability (PwBD), you get a massive 10 extra years, and that stacks with your category (so PwBD + SC = 15 extra years). Ex-servicemen also get relaxations based on the years they served plus 3 years. Always, always check the official PDF for the exact cutoff date they use to calculate your age. Sometimes they use January 1st, sometimes they use August 1st. It can literally make or break your eligibility.</p>

